-- title:
--   Coefficient certificates for G₁₅ under Klein's half-turn, part two
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\alpha,\beta,s \in K$ satisfy the four relations $\alpha\beta = -s$, $2\alpha^2 = -5-s$, $2\beta^2 = s-5$ and $s^2 = 5$. The conclusion is a conjunction of ten polynomial identities in $\alpha$ and $\beta$, each a sum of monomials $c\,\alpha^a\beta^b$ with explicit integer coefficients and with $a+b = 19$ throughout. Four of the identities have right-hand side $0$ (the second, third, fourth, seventh, eighth and ninth conjuncts, six in all), while the remaining four assert that the corresponding degree-$19$ expression equals a multiple of a single linear term: $482421875\,\alpha$ for the first, $-333984375\,\beta$ for the fifth, $-111328125\,\alpha$ for the sixth, and $1953125\,\beta$ for the tenth. No further hypotheses are imposed: the assertion is purely that these ten relations hold in any characteristic-zero field for any triple $(\alpha,\beta,s)$ subject to the four displayed constraints.
--
--   These are the normal forms of the coefficients of $u^{10},\dots,u^{19}$ arising when the binary form attached to the numerator $57u^{15}-247u^{10}-171u^5-1$ of the Rubin–Silverberg Möbius datum is substituted through Klein's half-turn generator $U = s^{-1}\begin{pmatrix}-\alpha & \beta\\ \beta & \alpha\end{pmatrix}$ of the binary icosahedral group, with $\alpha = \zeta-\zeta^4$, $\beta = \zeta^2-\zeta^3$, $s = \sqrt5$ for a primitive fifth root of unity $\zeta$; stating them over an abstract field subject to the four relations makes them a finite polynomial certificate. Together with the companion certificate for the lower-degree coefficients they feed the verification that $U$ acts as an icosahedral symmetry of the Rubin–Silverberg datum, which is used by [`RubinSilverberg.icoU_datumG`](thm.html#RubinSilverberg.icoU_datumG).
